 \label{eq:chaingamma}
\end{align}
To derive the gradient of $\mathsf{SE}$, we first obtain the gradient of $\mathsf{SE}_k$ and then sum the resulting per-user gradients over all users. Based on \eqref{eq:spectral}, $\mathsf{SE}_k$ can be reformulated as
